  "body": "## Review Finding\n\n**[P2] Resolve referenced parameter schemas before deriving scalar types.**  \n`_param_type` handles inline OpenAPI 3.x schemas, including the new 3.1 nullable forms, but it does not resolve a parameter schema such as `schema: {\"$ref\": \"#/components/schemas/CustomerId\"}`. OpenAPI permits Schema Objects to be references, so an integer, number, or boolean identifier defined in `components.schemas` is currently recorded as `string`. Both generated tool surfaces then advertise and validate the wrong type and can reject a correctly typed JSON value before dispatch. Pass the root specification into scalar-type extraction and resolve local schema references—or reuse an existing schema resolver—before falling back to `string`. [organon/src/organon/operation_config.pyL736-L752](https://github.com/Skrates/sokrates/blob/743c29799066cc1041c088e83057e387878c95f7/organon/src/organon/operation_config.py#L736-L752)\n\n**Checks**\n* ✅ `uv run --package organon pytest organon/tests/test_operation_config_generator.py organon/tests/test_pydantic_ai_tools.py organon/tests/test_tool_catalog_expanded.py -q` — 133 passed.\n* ✅ `uv run --package organon python - <<'PY' ... PY` — confirmed that `_param_type({\"schema\": {\"$ref\": \"#/components/schemas/CustomerId\"}})` currently returns `string`.\n* ✅ `git status --short --branch` — clean working tree; review only, so no code change, commit, or follow-up PR was created.\n\n [View task →](https://chatgpt.com/s/cd_6a895bb9cf5c8191b9f4e0ca32ad9e35)",
